; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Paper Pinwheel
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     triangle, rotation, filled, animation
; SUMMARY:  Builds a pinwheel from eight colored triangles and then makes it spin in the wind.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Eight triangles, each turned 45 degrees from the last, make
;   the blades of a paper pinwheel on a stick. Then the picture is
;   wiped and drawn again a little more turned, again and again,
;   so the pinwheel spins round.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch it spin. Change BLADES to 4, 6 or 12.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * one blade, repeated and turned, makes the whole pattern
;   * SETHEADING to start every drawing at a chosen angle
;   * animation: CLEAN, draw, WAIT, and draw again a bit different
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Make it spin the other way.
;   * Make it spin faster by turning more each time, or with a shorter WAIT.
;   * Use only two colors that take turns.
; ============================================================

make "blades 8
make "colors [[230 60 60] [250 200 40] [60 150 230] [80 190 100]]

; One blade is a right-angled triangle with a corner at the center.
to blade :size :color
  filled :color [
    forward :size
    right 135
    forward :size * 0.7
    setxy 0 60
  ]
end

; All the blades, starting at the angle :start.
; Later drawing covers earlier drawing, so the stick goes first and
; the blades are painted over its top end.
to pinwheel :start
  ; the stick is a long thin rectangle
  penup setxy -5 -270 setheading 0
  filled [150 110 70] [repeat 2 [forward 330 right 90 forward 10 right 90]]
  repeat :blades [
    penup setxy 0 60 setheading :start + 360 * repcount / :blades pendown
    blade 130 item 1 + remainder repcount count :colors :colors
  ]
  ; the pin in the middle is a dot, which sits on top
  setpensize 14 setpencolor [80 80 80]
  dot [0 60]
  setpensize 2 setpencolor [255 255 255]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [200 230 250]
setpensize 2 setpencolor [255 255 255]
; turn 3 degrees per picture, 360 pictures = three full turns
for [angle 0 1080 3] [
  clean
  pinwheel :angle
  wait 2
]
